"""Golden-frame snapshot regression lock for the M16 Task 2 OLED render.

Renders four canonical KrabState frames to ``to_ascii()`` and pins the EXACT
expected 128x64 output. This is the coarsest, strongest regression net: it
catches ANY pixel change, wherever it originates (glyphs, body tiling, battery,
face, text strip, geometry constants).

If one of these goldens fails, that is a SIGNAL, not a chore. Only regenerate a
golden when the render was DELIBERATELY changed (new glyph, moved region, font
swap). To regenerate, re-run the render for the failing state and paste the new
literal -- never regenerate blindly to make a red test green; first confirm the
pixel diff is exactly the change you intended.

Regenerate one frame with (cwd = krabby-research):

    PYTHONPATH=firmware/oled_sim testenv/bin/python -c \
        "from krab import KrabState, render; print(render(KrabState()).to_ascii())"

The companion structural tests assert the *why* (apex direction, region
occupancy); these goldens assert the *exact bytes*.
"""
